    genlmsg_cancel(msg, hdr);
    goto out;
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the function `batadv_iv_gw_dump` stops processing when `batadv_iv_gw_dump_entry` returns a non-zero value, which can happen even for invalid gateway entries. This leads to the potential of returning an empty message to userspace, causing the netlink dumping to halt prematurely and resulting in no gateway entries being sent, despite valid entries existing.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
int ret = 0; // Change initial return value to indicate success
```
```c
if (curr_gw == gw_node) {
    if (nla_put_flag(msg, BATADV_ATTR_FLAG_BEST)) {
        genlmsg_cancel(msg, hdr);
        goto out;
    }
}
```
Reason:
The fix changes the initial return value to `0`, indicating success instead of an error. This allows the processing to continue even if there are invalid entries, preventing the premature stopping of the netlink dumping process and ensuring that valid gateway entries can still be sent to userspace.

